[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"justify","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The justify attribute is used to indicate left, center, or right justification. The default value varies for different elements. For elements where the justify attribute is present but the halign attribute is not, the justify attribute indicates horizontal alignment as well as justification.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"halign","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"underline","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of lines used to underline the text: ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"overline","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of lines used to overline the text: ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"lineThrough","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of lines used to strike through the text: ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"rotation","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The rotation attribute is used to rotate text around the alignment point specified by the halign and valign attributes. Positive values are clockwise rotations, while negative values are counter-clockwise rotations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"letterSpacing","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The letter-spacing attribute specifies text tracking. Values are either “normal” or a number representing the number of ems to add between each letter. The number may be negative in order to subtract space. The default is normal, which allows flexibility of letter-spacing for purposes of text justification.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"lineHeight","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The line-height attribute specifies text leading. Values are either “normal” or a number representing the percentage of the current font height to use for leading. The default is “normal”. The exact normal value is implementation-dependent, but values between 100 and 120 are recommended.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"xmlLang","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The xml:lang attribute value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"xmlSpace","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The xml:space attribute value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"dir","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The text-direction attribute is used to adjust and override the Unicode bidirectional text algorithm, similar to the Directionality data category in the W3C Internationalization Tag Set recommendation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"enclosure","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The enclosure attribute group is used to specify the formatting of an enclosure around text or symbols.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLFormattedTextIDV2id5value7justify8position4font5color6halign6valign9underline8overline11lineThrough8rotation13letterSpacing0P6Height7xmlLang0V5Space3dir9enclosureACSSSg_SSAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgAA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgAyA9MXLValignOSgAA16MXLNumberOfLinesVSgA10_A10_SdSgAA17MXLNumberOrNormalOSgA14_AvA06MXLXmlX0OSgAA16MXLTextDirectionOSgAA17MXLEnclosureShapeOSgtcfc","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"justify","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{